WEBVTT

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.500
"EARTH DEFENSE FORCE
SAITAMA BRANCH"

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:21.910
Wake up! I'm hungry!
Get up!

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.790
Come on!

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.620
Oh, sorry.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.910
I have to get breakfast ready.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.580
It's past noon!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:39.120
After I helped you develop the XERO suits,
this is the way you treat me?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.120
I know. My bad.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.330
I can't wait
for Retto and the others to get back.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.200
Focus on lunch first!

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.580
Super HXEROS!

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.250
Episode 10: The Two Kiraras!

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.580
Well, let's go, everyone.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.870
Any HERO worth their salt needs to come
to this town when they visit Tokyo.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.580
I know what you mean!

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.790
Ichogi seems really excited about this.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.540
Is she an Akihibara regular?

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.620
Looks like it.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.580
Well, shall we?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.370
Where should we go first?

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.870
Wait a second!

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:21.120
Tourists or not, wandering around in a big group
is both embarrassing and gets in people's way.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.750
So why don't we split up into two groups?

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.330
You have a point.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.620
I guess a group of four and one of five?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.660
How about this?

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.790
The members, highest H-energy scores
to lowest, choose which team they're on.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.160
No, thanks.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.160
That's embarrassing,
and I don't want to share my score.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.500
I agree. Why don't we decide
with rock-paper-scissors?

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.410
Yeah.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.160
One, two, three,
rock-paper-scissors!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.450
So we'll show these three around.
See you later.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.620
Okay. We'll give these two the tour.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.750
Why is Moena the leader?

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.370
Because of you,
Enjo ended up with the other group.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:11.620
Shut up. You're the one who had
the big idea of splitting up into groups.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.750
See? Even you think it's a mistake.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.120
I-I don't know what you mean.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.870
Somewhere along the line,
those two have become friends.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.620
Works for me. It's been too long since you
and I got to talk one-on-one, Momocchi.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.290
That doesn't do anything for me.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.120
So where are we heading?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.330
Somewhere that will make you two happy.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.200
Then I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.330
Good. I wonder where
the other group is going.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.790
Good question.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:52.160
"OWL CAFE"

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.950
A-Adorable!

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:02.700
I never thought I'd get to meet an owl
close up in the heart of Tokyo.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.290
Cat cafes and maid coffee shops are fine,

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.200
but this kind of niche shop
is what makes Akihibara so cool.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.410
Now, I know that owls
have various expressions.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.040
And their hoots are so soft and soothing.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.120
Look at this!

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.410
This owl is like you, Coach!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.660
Really?

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.540
The one next to it reminds me of Hoshino.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.250
I'll show it to Hoshino on the way home.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.870
Enjo and Hoshino seem very close.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:38.290
N-No, not that close.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.790
I was talking about the owls.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.040
Oh, that's what you meant.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.370
If I didn't mishear,

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.410
I came with because you said
you wanted to go to a HERO shop.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.910
But there's no "H" in this shop!

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:02.080
In the first place,
I'm sure minors aren't allowed in here!

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.120
It's fine, Kirarin.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:08.450
The first floor is just gag gifts.
The adult stuff is upstairs.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:13.250
Yeah, maybe you should buy some stuff
in case of an emergency, Kirara.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:16.160
Hey, keep that junk away from me!

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.540
I'm going to get some fresh air!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:21.830
She escaped.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.200
That was embarrassing.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.120
Wh-What the...

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.540
Murasame!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.910
What is that?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.910
I'm surprised someone so innocent
can be a member of the HXEROS.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.620
From what I saw
over the last couple of days,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.250
your relationship with Retto Enjo
hasn't evolved at all.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.790
Wh-What about it?

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.660
That settles it.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:56.250
My mind is made up, Kirara Hoshino.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:00.540
Next time,
I'm going to seriously seduce Retto Enjo.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.250
Well, I got what I came for,
so now I'm going home.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:13.200
Don't slack off. We might not
be the only ones targeting him.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.410
A-Am I in a pinch here?

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.950
Where are you, Sora?

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.910
Hime, over here!

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.540
Akihibara even has a place like this.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.910
This is my first time here, too.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:37.660
That looks fun!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.580
Virtual Heroines.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.500
Are you interested in that kind of thing?

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.250
Ichogi!

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:56.120
In this VR game, your childhood friend
who lives next door is helping you study.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.500
Childhood friend?

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.370
It's totally realistic!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.700
Since we're here, give it a try.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.290
A-All right, just for a bit.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.620
What do you see, Enjo?

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:15.830
A classroom
and one of those girls from out there.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:19.330
So far, so good.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.160
Actually, this game
is only ostensibly about studying.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.750
It heats up
when you start flirting with the girl.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:28.000
But I bet he won't be satisfied
with VR alone.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:35.580
Recently, VR even gives you
a realistic tactile experience.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.120
It's like you're really there.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.200
Wait. Enjo...

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.040
What'll I do if that really happens?

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.200
Wow. It looks like there's
a real girl in front of me.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:56.950
What am I doing?

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:00.080
This makes me a pervert!

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.700
Look at that...

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.500
That's right. This is my H-energy.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.950
At school and home, I'm a model student.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:14.200
After getting tired of that lifestyle,
I was invited to join HXEROS.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.950
But even there, the other members
have the sex appeal,

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.290
while I became the coordinator.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.500
Yay!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.160
My H-energy...

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.700
I feel so immoral!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.000
I heard a weird sound.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.540
Did something happen?

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.370
Ichogi?

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:42.330
Um, I can explain.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:47.120
D-Don't tell anyone about this.
I'm begging you.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.200
Begging me for what?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:52.580
Um, actually,
I already like this one girl,

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:56.120
so even if that was a joke,
please don't do it again.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.450
Maybe you got the wrong idea, Enjo.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.290
That's not how I feel about you.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.660
Y-You don't do this kind of thing
with the other members in Saitama?

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.870
Of course not.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.450
She tricked me!

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:17.830
Murasame told me all of the teams
collect H-energy this way!

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:19.370
As if!

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:23.330
I'm really sorry!
I didn't mean it like that!

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:26.000
Okay, I more or less get the picture.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.660
But, Saitama Branch is incredible.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.250
I don't know if you're serious or pure.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:34.950
Even without doing that stuff,

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:39.160
your Kiseichuu-slaying abilities
are first-class.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.040
In a normal person's eyes,
Tokyo Branch must be weird.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.080
I don't think you're weird.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.450
I don't think any HERO worries about what
other people are thinking when they fight.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:54.120
Thank you. Hearing that makes me think
I can endure the embarrassment.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.410
Maybe...

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.250
I'm a little envious of the girl who likes you.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.450
Well, thanks for today.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:08.200
No, thank you!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:15.200
Sorry. I have to go to the bathroom,
so you can go on ahead.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.750
Okay.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.750
--If you get lost, we'll leave you behind.
--Gotcha!

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:23.620
What's she talking about?
Like I'd get lost so easily.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.500
Crap. I'm lost.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.620
I'm as bad as the rest
when it comes to sense of direction.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.160
Enjo?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.330
Huh? Where are Momozono and the others?

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:45.080
There were so many people
that we got separated.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:47.120
The same as me.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:52.040
--Hey, why don't we go home together?
--Hey, why don't we go home together?

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:55.330
Bam! Happochuu!

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:04.660
I'm a little envious of the girl who likes you.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.790
Next time, I'm going
to seriously seduce Retto Enjo.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.750
--I'd better say something.
--I'd better say something.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:17.250
Oh, right. We went to this owl cafe,
and there was an owl that resembled you.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.330
I took a photo. Want to see it?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.540
Huh. That's cute.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.830
But I think I like
the one next to it better.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:30.620
Huh? I have a feeling
that one reminds me of somebody.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.830
O-Oh, right!
Where did your group end up going today?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.580
Me?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.620
Nowhere especially interesting, honestly.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.950
So you say,
but you bought something there.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.540
It's something a member
of Tokyo Branch left behind!

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.830
The train is about to depart.
Please wait a moment.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.330
H-Hey, we'd better get off here!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.910
I'm sorry!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.700
I'm getting off!

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.950
That was close.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.910
I'm just glad
you realized it was our stop.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:07.910
Hoshino, what happened
to your hair ornament?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:12.450
Huh? Maybe it fell off
when I bumped into that person.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.080
What should I do?

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:18.660
I'll ask the station staff if we can look for it
when the train reaches the end of the line!

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.500
You don't have to do that.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:26.580
I could just buy
another one of the same type.

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:30.910
How long have I had
that hair ornament?

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.910
Even though I've worn it nearly every day,
I can't remember where I got it.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:40.700
I have a feeling that hair ornament
was really important to me.

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.450
Finally found it.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:50.200
Thank you!

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.620
I'm glad you found it.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.330
If it's a present from your boyfriend,
well, you wouldn't want to lose that.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.830
I-It's not that!

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.330
Sorry. It's none of my business.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:04.910
Listen, it's getting late.
Why don't we call your parents?

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:07.540
No, we're fine.

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:14.580
At times like these,
the man takes the lead.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.660
Well...

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:24.200
There aren't any trains till morning,
so why don't we have your uncle pick us up?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.700
Yeah.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.910
Hey, Enjo...

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:48.830
Do you know something
about this hair ornament?

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:54.660
My memories from around the time we
were attacked by that Kiseichuu are fuzzy.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.330
I can't remember how long I've had this.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.540
If you're hiding something,
tell me what it is!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.500
I-It's no big thing.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:10.040
Besides, if you can't remember,
maybe it's a memory you don't want to recall.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.660
Maybe Dark Kirara would know,
but for some reason,

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:17.830
I have a feeling
that I'd better not ask her.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.660
So...

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.250
Please tell me.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.330
All right.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:29.790
But don't tell anyone else,
especially Momozono.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.500
It's embarrassing to talk about
after all this time,

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.790
but actually,
I gave you that hair ornament.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.660
No way!

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:48.540
But what's the connection
with the Kiseichuu?

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:52.450
I-I have a feeling...

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:56.040
...it's because it was my proposal present.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:01.450
Good morning, Ret!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:02.830
Morning, Hoshino!

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.080
Wasn't it hot last night?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:09.500
Look, I didn't wear much when I went
to bed, so I got a mosquito bite here.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:12.950
Idiot! Don't show me your chest
on the way to school!

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:18.290
So you don't mind,
as long as it isn't on the way to school.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.410
Shut up.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.290
Hey, which do you think it was?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.620
Don't know! Don't care!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.290
Sheesh, she always teases me.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:29.410
On top of that,
she's a selfish smart-aleck!

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:33.620
But that's the Hoshino I loved.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:38.200
It's her birthday,
the day I finally take the initiative.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.870
See you later.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.120
What is it, Retto?

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.540
You wanted to meet me here?

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.160
And this letter...

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.910
"MARRY ME. I'LL BE WAITING BEHIND
THE GYM AFTER SCHOOL. BY RETTO"

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.870
Are you serious about this?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.160
Well, yeah.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.660
She fell for it!

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.370
That's right.
It looks like I wrote "Marry me,"

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:09.000
but I actually wrote "Battle me"!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:14.250
Huh. So that's how you think of me!

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:19.000
I wrote "battle"!
What did you misread it as?

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:27.330
The perfect plan to get back at Hoshino
by having her misread it as "marry"!

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:31.620
Go ahead. Mess with me as usual, Hoshino!

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:35.660
W-Well, if that's what you want, Ret.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:44.660
But I think we're
a little young for marriage...

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.370
...you know?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.580
Huh? What is this mood?

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.750
This isn't what I expected.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.040
Knowing Hoshino,
there's got to be more to it.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.700
She must be plotting something!

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.700
Th-That's right. Here!

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.790
It's your birthday, right?

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:03.040
This is for you.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:06.450
Put it on
once you have an answer to my letter.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.330
After taking it this far,
she's gotta have a comeback line.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:14.750
Come on.
Show me your true colors, Hoshino!

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:20.750
Thank you. I'll take good care of this.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.910
I-I lose, Hoshino.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.950
Oh, that's right.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:35.540
A little disappointed?

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.040
Keep quiet.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:40.200
But how can you consider that a proposal?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:43.750
W-Well, the way you reacted to it...

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.000
Some time after our encounter
with the Kiseichuu,

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:53.500
I saw you were wearing it and asked
if you wanted to go home together.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:58.040
Save your jokes. The only thing that's
funny about you is your lousy writing.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:00.620
Wh-What?

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:05.450
At the time, I couldn't figure out
why you suddenly hated me.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:08.660
But I see. You forgot about it.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:15.200
I can't believe my memory of the present
is gone along with that first Kiseichuu!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.120
Did I buy this hair ornament?

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:22.500
Oh, well. It's cute, so I'll put it on.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.000
Then...

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:30.080
All this time, I've been engaged to Enjo?

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.330
Even that time, and that time?

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.500
I'm so embarrassed,
I wanna crawl into a hole!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.040
Why has something so trivial
driven you into a tizzy?

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:41.000
When he's seen you in so many
other embarrassing positions...

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.450
Jeez, why didn't you
tell me about it earlier?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.580
When it meant I was giving
my okay to that note...

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.580
You're more carefree than I thought.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.870
Y-You're finally talking to me
on the regular!

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.750
What was that?

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:06.620
Maybe a Kiseichuu?

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.950
It's probably a cat or something.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.950
I-Is there a cat type?

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.120
No, I'm not talking about Kiseichuu!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.790
A raccoon dog!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.660
What's it doing here?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.700
No, that's a common raccoon.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:37.330
How cute!

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.250
It seems tame. Come over here!

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:43.410
No, that's dangerous!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.870
It ran away.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.620
I-I didn't see anything.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.290
It's not what you think!

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.120
Like I said before,
Murasame left this behind,

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:03.290
so I'll give it back to her next time!

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:07.830
B-But couldn't you have given it
to Wakakusa instead?

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.290
Now that he mentions it...

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:12.200
Well, there's nothing wrong with that.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.950
This shows that you finally have
a HERO's sensibilities.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.120
Stop jumping to conclusions!

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.540
Ow! I-I was kidding!

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.620
If you take it that seriously...

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:30.620
I-I tried to warn you.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.620
Here. You can borrow my jacket. Put it on.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.620
I think she's gone.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.790
Sorry for suddenly...

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.910
Nah, your instinct saved us.

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:04.870
Even though it was on impulse,
I can't believe I did that!

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:09.950
Am I shaken up after Retto reminded me
of what happened back then?

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:12.330
The day we were attacked by a Kiseichuu...

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:15.580
I never wanted to think
about that embarrassing memory again,

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:18.410
to the point
where I kept all boys at a distance.

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:21.200
And yet, it's like
I'm back where I started.

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:25.580
But if I have to encounter
the Kiseichuu...

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:27.450
Come to think of it...

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:32.200
I guess I never did give you
a proper answer.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:37.330
Oh, that was just a youthful indiscretion,
so there's no need to...

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:42.160
But then it's like I can't even respond
when someone confesses their love to me!

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:44.330
O-Oh?

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:50.160
So if our relationship can go back to being
what it was before we saw the Kiseichuu...

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:53.950
If we're able to exterminate
every last Kiseichuu...

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:57.700
I'll give you my answer then.

00:22:57.700 --> 00:22:59.040
But...

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:03.410
If you fall for another girl before then,
I'll never forgive you.

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:05.500
Huh? What is this?

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:08.750
Is she actually saying...

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.700
No, hold on. I've gotta calm down.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:12.830
Is it even possible?

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:17.040
F-For now, I'll call my uncle!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.370
The call you are attempting to make
cannot be completed.

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:25.450
Sounds like he forgot to charge his phone.

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:27.580
Then, what do we do?

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.250
No choice.

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:38.160
At times like these,
the man takes the lead.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:44.410
Shall we take a taxi home?

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.200
Super HXEROS!

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:51.910
Next time: Bye-bye, HXEROS!
